  "body": "## What changed\n- `assets/posts/sinker-iso.cps`: `onOpen` takes inch/mm from `postOptions.Units` (the document's unit, #902), no longer from `machine.units`; the manifest declares `programUnits = \"mm inch\"`, as `wire-iso.cps` does. Lengths and feeds already went through `fu`/`ff`, and the unit word is the machine's `edm.codes.metric` / `edm.codes.inch`, so an inch document on a machine that states no inch code is refused by name (\"states no edm.codes.inch\").\n- `crates/post/tests/script_sinker_iso.rs`: new pinning test; the existing missing-inch-code refusal now asks an inch *document* instead of an inch machine file.\n\n## How tested\n- Pinning test `the_sinker_program_posts_in_the_documents_unit_not_the_machine_files` (camcraft-post, `script_sinker_iso`): an inch machine file under an mm document (and with no unit stated) posts the mm golden byte for byte; an inch document on the mm fixture writes `G20` in place of `G21` and every X/Y/Z/H/F / 25.4, everything else equal (`M100 H0.5906`, `M101 Z0.5531`). Fails on the old post (\"an inch machine file must not make an inch program\").\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_sinker_iso`: 22/22.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test program_units --test sinker_burn --test conformance`: 7/7, 14/14, 7/7 (`no_shipped_post_takes_the_program_unit_from_the_machine_file` green again).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No real EDM control; no inch sinker golden committed (the inch program is checked word by word against the mm golden in the test). Full batch tier not run (targeted only).\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM (ISO) post writes the program in the document's unit (G20/G21 from the machine's edm codes), never the machine file's unit\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1382\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
